  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only scvi multiprofile is the strongest direction, with validation accuracy around 0.65 and F1 around 0.63, while image-only ResNet50 is weak, reaching only about 0.33 accuracy with multiprofile avgpool. The key uncertainty is whether a stronger image representation, ImageNet ViT-L, contains useful signal before spending budget on multimodal fusion. config_014 keeps profile=multiprofile and aggregation=avgpool, matching the completed image ResNet50 multiprofile avgpool experiment, so it cleanly isolates the effect of image encoder representation. This is the best next experiment because it is informative even if its immediate accuracy may be lower than the current RNA-only best: if ViT-L alone improves substantially, a multimodal scvi+ViT extension becomes well justified; if it remains weak, multimodal experiments relying on poor image features are less attractive."
}

